# Project-specific: large/regeneratable/licensing-sensitive artifacts
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/chunks/
data/index/

# LLM evaluation phase (docs/evaluation-design.md, ADR-0010/0011, added
# 2026-07-24): these files carry real cited/retrieved chunk excerpts
# (verbatim corpus text) -- same licensing sensitivity as data/chunks/
# above, decided before the first push per ADR-0011's own consequence
# list. Only the slim, excerpt-free CSVs (judgment_id/question_id/
# category/verdict/reason/human_verdict, no chunk text) and the final
# markdown report are committed.
data/eval/generation_results.jsonl
data/eval/judgments.jsonl
data/eval/contradiction_search_results.json
data/eval/*_full.csv
# Added 2026-07-25, Prompt A/B comparison (compare_prompts.py): same
# reasoning as generation_results.jsonl/judgments.jsonl above -- these
# two also carry real cited/retrieved chunk excerpts. Found not yet
# gitignored (existing entries only matched the two exact filenames
# above, not these) before either was ever committed -- caught via
# `git check-ignore` while writing this session's reports.md, not after
# a push. The aggregate-only prompt-comparison-report.md IS committed,
# same split as the original generation-evaluation-report.md.
data/eval/prompt_comparison_results.jsonl
data/eval/prompt_comparison_judgments.jsonl
# Added 2026-07-25, human-calibration correction: this file carries full
# cited_chunk_texts (verbatim corpus excerpts) same as the *_full.csv
# files above, but its name doesn't match that wildcard -- same class of
# gap as the prompt_comparison files just above, caught the same way
# (git check-ignore, before any push) rather than after the fact.
data/eval/human_calibration_disagreement_subset.csv
# Added 2026-07-25, judge rubric v2 full re-run: same reasoning as
# judgments.jsonl above -- carries real cited chunk excerpts. Checked with
# git check-ignore before writing this session's reports.md rather than
# assuming the existing judgments.jsonl entry covered it (it didn't, same
# gap class as the two entries just above).
data/eval/judgments_v2.jsonl
# Added 2026-07-25, redesigned human-calibration review artifact
# (scripts/build_calibration_review_v2.py): the HTML page embeds full
# verbatim cited-excerpt text for all 65 calibration rows, same licensing
# sensitivity as the *_full.csv files above -- same gap class, checked
# with git check-ignore before claiming it in reports.md. The companion
# data/eval/human_calibration_v2_verdicts.csv is NOT excluded here: it's
# the slim judgment_id/human_verdict file, no excerpt text, same split as
# judge_calibration_sample.csv vs. judge_calibration_sample_full.csv.
data/eval/human_calibration_review_v2.html

# ADR-0016 (GCP cloud deployment, 2026-07-26): Dockerfile.cloud, when
# built, bakes Freedom House + Access Now's real rehydrated text directly
# into an image -- unlike the public Dockerfile (repo root), which only
# ever bakes the licensing-clear 54% tiered baseline (ADR-0013). Freedom
# House's permission request is still open (ADR-0013's own revisit
# condition) -- this must never reach the public repo or any release
# artifact, only a private Artifact Registry repo in Sam's own GCP
# project (deploy/gcp-deploy.sh). Flagged explicitly in reports.md,
# 2026-07-26, for a second look -- this is a judgment call (the file
# itself carries no corpus text, only instructions to fetch it at build
# time), not a certainty.
#
# src/interface/entrypoint.cloud.sh and Dockerfile.grafana.cloud are
# deliberately NOT listed here -- neither bakes or references any
# rehydrated content or secret; they're just the cloud runtime command
# and Grafana provisioning config, safe to stay public.
Dockerfile.cloud

